{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1545620-future-sight","id":1545620,"title":"Future sight","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-09T09:19:38-08:00","id":1545620,"title":"Future sight","content":"Lets say a mage casts a spell that lets him see a few seconds in the future. How do you deal with this as a ST?<br /> If you tell the character what happens before it happens he can almost never be surprized and can analise any trap just observing how he dies in one and then deciding not to do it. Is that even a problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-09T09:42:19-08:00","id":1545621,"title":"","content":"One way is simply playing out the next few seconds, then jumping back to the point the spell was cast and playing it again. It\u2019s cumbersome but it gives the exact kind of information the spell would.<br /> <br /> A quicker alternative I would steal from the Powered by the Apocalypse system is describe a general sequence of events, then give reduced difficulty on moves made in the next few seconds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T07:34:49-08:00","id":1545934,"title":"","content":"Just let the PC know what the NPCs will do and act accordingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-09T22:52:34-07:00","id":1559319,"title":"","content":"Just because you can see it coming, doesn't necessarily mean you're fast enough to do anything about it.<br /> <br /> Or you might have just enough time to make a single change to the course of events, like rescue the closest victim from danger, while being unable to reach the others.<br /> <br /> Make it a selling point that this isn't a convenient power to counter any threat coming your way. If the spell only lets you see glimpses into the immediate future, then the user has to make spit second decisions in the heat of the moment. Not plan out elaborate strategies ahead of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-10T00:58:56-07:00","id":1559320,"title":"","content":"If it's like &quot;enough seconds you can see the next round of combat&quot;, the ST can inform the player what NPCs <i>intend</i> to do. (Since, much like quantum stuff, observing the future changes the future, because you're acting to preempt it).<br /> <br /> You could make it even simpler, by just giving the PC blanket reductions to difficulty for things like dodging attacks or aiming. On such short notice, the PC is mainly focusing on how their view of the immediate future can best factor into any person's two big concerns in a fight: 1) not dying and 2) eliminating or evading the guys trying to make you die. The rest can be handwaved.<br /> <br /> (If you want the ability to get and process more information about the battlefield, this is where a conjunctional Mind 1 rider to your Time 2 effect would come in handy. Allowing you to do &quot;multi-track thinking&quot;, in a way normal people can't. So you're both reacting to the important bits, while also keeping an eye on broader aspects of the fight, like where NPCs are moving or that one of them will try to make off with the MacGuffin.)<br /> <br /> If it's a non-combat use of Foresight, it's dependent on the situation. If you were about to blunder into a landmine, the ST just tells you, &quot;you have a vision of stepping on something, hearing a click, and your legs getting blown off&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}